Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[" Section 3.3", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"d6413e2a-75dd-4d7d-bb99-be83e47d4803"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["  Liapunov Functions",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"35c97960-17ec-4d0b-a75d-\
da6f6e039ba7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Remove", "[", "\"\<Global`*\>\"", " ", "]"}], " "}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398352136171*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1220]:=",ExpressionUUID->"404beec7-d728-4f41-bc25-aa1c74f40050"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Introduction", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"eadf5fe3-5b60-474d-bdc9-2ac9ff1442d2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To summarize what we have accomplished:\n\nWe considered a second order \
ODE.\n\nWe expressed the second order ODE as a first order system  (Position \
and velocity).\n\nThen we examined the resulting vector field for the first \
order system and observed that the solutions of the ODE system would follow \
the vector field.\n          \nThus, we are now motivated to study the \
relationship between the solutions of an ODE, the corresponding vector field \
for the first order system.  In addition, we will examine an extension of the \
idea of total energy (potential plus kinetic) which will determine if an \
equilibrium point is an attractor.  \nThe conceptual idea is quite simple:\n\t\
 For a simple dynamic system such as the pendulum problem or the mass-spring \
problem, the total energy of the system is a combination of both the \
potential and kinetic energies. The potential energy is usually a function of \
position (spring displacement for the mass-spring problem and angular \
displacement for the pendulum problem).  The kinetic energy is usually a \
function of velocity.  If the dynamic system experiences no losses, then the \
total energy remains constant.  For this case, orbits in the phase plane \
neither expand nor contract ( i.e. stable, but the equilibrium point is not \
an attractor).  However, if the dynamic system experiences losses (by \
friction for the mass-spring problem and by viscous damping for the pendulum) \
then the total energy will decrease with time.  For this case, a solution \
orbit will be attracted to the equilibrium position (i.e. stable).  However, \
if the dynamic system continually gains energy (by some process that \
transfers energy from the outside to the dynamic system), then the total \
energy will increase with time.  For this case, a solution orbit will \
continue to expand away from an equilibrium position (i.e. unstable).\n\t \
Therefore, what we would like to do is extend the idea of conservation of \
energy to more general systems.  A function that plays a role equivalent to \
total energy is called a Liapunov function.  The behavior of the Liapunov \
function was described above:\n\t If it decreases along an orbit, then the \
equilibrium point is asymptotically stable\n\t If it is constant along an \
orbit, then the equilibrium is stable but not asymptotically stable\n\t If it \
increases along an orbit, then the equilibrium point is unstable\n In \
summary, we want to find a function V[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["X", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "079f020f-d14a-4ba6-a2c5-9ba05c866b51"],
 "] such that:\n \t V[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["X", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c1a3a85e-7d19-4ca8-a1d1-483bb5c54578"],
 "] = 0  where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["X", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f1759fc6-08e7-4322-819c-788ac400997a"],
 " is an isolated equilibrium point (i.e. no remaining energy at the rest \
point).\n \t V[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "25123e3a-a662-495c-bfad-aff16f8e73d0"],
 "] \[GreaterEqual] 0   (i.e. total energy is non-negative).\n\t ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"V", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        FormBox[
         OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
         TraditionalForm], "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
    "\[LessEqual]", "  ", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "51d40fcf-4fe7-446f-b235-27d15ae99994"],
 "  along an orbit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
     TraditionalForm], "[", "t", "]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "185d34ad-0969-46df-978e-551946850eca"],
 " (i.e. total energy decreases or remains constant in time).\nFinally, \
observe that there may be many different Liapunov functions."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7300437b-0120-4cca-86f8-474837fd7cbe"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Construction of Liapunov Functions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4e10cf94-7c78-4c9a-ab75-891998299c8d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In short, a Liapunov function V[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0046fbde-1868-495b-8e03-c408ac21956a"],
 "], ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c26b76c5-0c78-41c1-9307-dd58e1108096"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {"x1"},
      {"x2"}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cf0e98dc-5f7c-45ad-aa0a-7d1dff243c16"],
 " is one which:\n \t V[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["X", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "bd50dc87-1a67-4e57-badd-af27dc38c071"],
 "] = 0  where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["X", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "10222011-7931-4d51-a7c6-c3710f3a98eb"],
 "= ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox["x1", "0"]},
      {
       SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d4683b5b-89d8-499e-ba86-3732749c14f3"],
 " is an isolated equilibrium point\n \t V[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8660b420-4d33-4fde-bcd7-cd14499a52a1"],
 "] \[GreaterEqual] 0   \n\t ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"V", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        FormBox[
         OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
         TraditionalForm], "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
    "\[LessEqual]", "  ", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a11c3b5c-80ed-4873-b30c-b1a91436ef97"],
 "  along orbits ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
     TraditionalForm], "[", "t", "]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7c557b25-323a-456a-8f26-3a0c39888126"],
 " inside an appropriate region \[CapitalOmega]\nThe last condition is \
equivalent to:\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"V", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       FormBox[
        OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
        TraditionalForm], "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"23a014d5-6b19-44b6-8ca4-c56ad17fa81e"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"V", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      FormBox[
       OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
       TraditionalForm], "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"22a64c5e-38a9-4467-9a95-8c521641a54d"],
 " = (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"V", "[", 
     FormBox[
      OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
      TraditionalForm], "]"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a2f32df3-b4d6-42b3-91e3-aa71b5d0360d"],
 ") * x1'[t] + (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"V", "[", 
     FormBox[
      OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
      TraditionalForm], "]"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "757c8c49-3de7-44e2-b483-8b2eefe1877c"],
 ") * x2'[t]    \[LessEqual]  0"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398352855557*^9},ExpressionUUID->"27be1c82-8535-42a4-b64c-d866a557b791"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
   RowBox[{"V", "[", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "]"}]}], "   ", "\[LessEqual]", 
  "  ", "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1221]:=",ExpressionUUID->"44fac868-e6a0-4bb3-8bb8-4071c31a3c74"],

Cell["Or, in traditional form:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cd3ff761-9656-4407-b1a8-42d48c960a19"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"V", "[", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "]"}]}], " ", "\[LessEqual]", 
   "  ", "0"}], "  ", "//", "TraditionalForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1222]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1b2b8bf0-770a-4343-955b-a11f5f0f7402"],

Cell["\<\
Fact:    For a time independent vector field, two distinctive orbits can \
never intersect as t \[Rule] \[Infinity].  Observe that the orbit starting at \
an equilibrium point can never move from the location (i.e. the solution \
orbit is constant).  One consequence of this is that an orbit starting at a \
non-equilibrium point can never reach the equilibrium point in a finite \
amount of time (Otherwise this orbit would intersect the constant orbit of \
the equilibrium point).
  
Define an invariant set in the domain to be one for which any orbit that \
begins in this set remains within it for all future time.  Example, any \
equilibrium point is invariant. Also, if R is any subset of the domain which \
contains no invariant subsets, then whenever an orbit enters the set R it \
must leave again after a finite amount of time.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e367dd6b-191f-4fee-995e-30b9a4816a5b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Theorem 3.4", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"8c96e0ab-6e15-498a-a9a1-f541d5963c74"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["X", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "da575018-5c55-4049-9d98-2686876c1f30"],
 " be an isolated equilibrium point of the ODE system:    \n\t  \t   x1' = \
f1[x1,x2]\n\t \t   x2' = f2[x1,x2]    \n   in some open subset \
\[CapitalOmega] of the domain.     \n   Assume that there exist V[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a25019ae-39bc-460c-bcb2-0bc3ed20a021"],
 "], a Liapunov function on \[CapitalOmega].   \n   Then, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["X", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4403071c-a48c-4646-8465-b9e8d9cfcd20"],
 " is an attractor (i.e. is stable).\n   \n    Furthermore: Suppose R is \
defined to be the subset of \[CapitalOmega] in which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"V", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      FormBox[
       OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
       TraditionalForm], "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"6f453eef-5a22-4745-8f59-3e3ee58e025b"],
 "  = 0, for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
     TraditionalForm], "[", "t", "]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4b1fe53e-e5ee-4678-a92a-b276c6ed9ba8"],
 " inside \[CapitalOmega].    \n    If R contains no invariant subsets other \
than the equilibrium point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["X", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c53087c9-1a28-40fe-a4b8-5662f56cb54f"],
 " itself, then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["X", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0832f22c-2c6f-4dd8-8b2b-71fea1d2175c"],
 " is an asymptotically stable equilibrium point.\n          \n       (For an \
outline of the proof see the book)\n       \nThus, one way to study stability \
is to find a Liapunov function and analyze its behavior in the vicinity of an \
equilibrium point."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398352175814*^9, 3.398352187782*^9}, {3.398352864748*^9,
   3.398352866514*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6293a163-33cf-4768-9b98-86d3b282f077"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Example: Mass-Spring System With Damping", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8d83b70b-a455-4a40-92ae-9f0d5aab4212"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the mass-spring problem and the pendulum problem, the total energy can \
be used as a Liapunov function.  Both of these problems can be expressed as a \
second-order ODE of the form: \n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"p", "''"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"r", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"p", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"f", "[", 
      RowBox[{"p", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "=", " ", "0"}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"d5c8d722-4bf6-4599-854b-c22e2e666af2"],
 "\nwhere ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"p", "[", "t", "]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0d114317-7400-4b92-b300-5fed1edebbdf"],
 " would correspond to the displacement for the mass-spring problem or the \
angular displacement for the pendulum problem.\nHowever, we will only \
consider the ",
 StyleBox["mass-spring problem",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " which is linear:\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"r", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["k1", "m"], 
      RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], " ", "=", " ", "0"}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b9589d86-c60b-49f1-a37d-cefdfb396ad2"],
 "\nMultiply this equation by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ab7d3956-4f73-4b1f-b345-2c146f220360"],
 " (which corresponds to the velocity):\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"r", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        FractionBox["k1", "m"], 
        RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], " ", "=", " ", "0"}], ")"}], "*", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3f6ae8eb-c9f6-416c-b238-19d84ed676ae"],
 "\nand put the friction term on the right hand side:\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        FractionBox["k1", "m"], 
        RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], " ", ")"}], "*", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], 
   StyleBox["=",
    FontWeight->"Bold"], " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", " ", "r"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], 
    StyleBox["*",
     FontWeight->"Bold"], 
    StyleBox[" ",
     FontWeight->"Bold"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}],
     FontWeight->"Bold"]}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"a5cd1943-5cd9-45c3-84f0-bcd344b9065d"],
 "\nand integrate:\n",
 StyleBox["\t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox["k1", "m"], 
         RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], " ", ")"}], "*", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], 
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}]}],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], 
   StyleBox["=",
    FontWeight->"Bold"], " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", " ", "r"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], 
     StyleBox["*",
      FontWeight->"Bold"], 
     StyleBox[" ",
      FontWeight->"Bold"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}],
      FontWeight->"Bold"], 
     RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}]}]}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"9bfb77b2-473c-438e-96b9-aca69cd32bb5"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398352876139*^9, 
  3.398352906605*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8cfdc47a-9720-45c6-8176-caa77cfb4856"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        FractionBox["k1", "m"], 
        RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], " ", ")"}],
     FontWeight->"Bold"], 
    StyleBox["*",
     FontWeight->"Bold"], 
    StyleBox[" ",
     FontWeight->"Bold"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}],
     FontWeight->"Bold"], 
    RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}]}], 
  StyleBox["==",
   FontWeight->"Bold"], " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", " ", "r"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], 
    StyleBox["*",
     FontWeight->"Bold"], 
    StyleBox[" ",
     FontWeight->"Bold"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}],
     FontWeight->"Bold"], 
    RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1223]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ab0b6e4a-284b-4a95-b185-15d7ddc6bfaa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One interpretation of this expression for a mechanical system is that: \n\t\
\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "2"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Prime]",
       MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "2"]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "376a198b-1540-4494-8b67-921c37a82bdf"],
 " \t\tis related to the kinetic energy \n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"k1", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], "2"]}], 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "m"}]],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b426ea55-aaed-477a-9424-99bea6e43140"],
 "    \t\tis related to the potential energy\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "r"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "2"], 
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}]}]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cacf7d46-3759-407f-aefe-4aab6bf0928b"],
 " \tis related to the frictional losses\nThis is just a reformulation of the \
conservation of energy.\n\nTherefore, take the Liapunov function to be:\n\t \t\
 V[x,x'] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"k1", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "m"}]], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["1", "2"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Prime]",
        MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "2"]}]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4bb2488b-3302-4a23-8b03-8d5e173df357"],
 "\nThen V satisfies the 3 conditions to be a Liapunov function:\n\t \t \
V[0,0] = 0  where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["X", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4e2f5995-9038-4d54-a149-b2569aa5ba0c"],
 "= ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {"0"},
      {"0"}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "83c6f4f7-913c-4525-b3c9-00c9529ffd9d"],
 " is an isolated equilibrium point\n\t \t V[x,x'] \[GreaterEqual] 0   \n\t\t \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"V", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", " ", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
    "\[LessEqual]", "  ", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c45d9a10-331f-4702-b386-0db43275f09d"],
 "  along orbits ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
     TraditionalForm], "[", "t", "]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b1d09b79-3c70-46d5-a553-df63fce95fc4"],
 " inside an appropriate region \[CapitalOmega]"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398352915472*^9, 
  3.398352927928*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"726d3f5c-2341-4d43-977e-bc23d58b943b"],

Cell["In order to verify this, let:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"832bfe40-46cf-46af-9cdd-07d6e11340a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"V", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x_", ",", "y_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"k1", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}], 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "m"}]], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "2"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["y", "2"]}]}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1224]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1a7a4a1c-bb3f-4d21-a618-3e0fe6687a7e"],

Cell["Therefore V = 0 at the equilibrium point:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d9d063bd-5302-44fa-a655-80da0d136664"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"V", "[", 
  RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1225]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c75360df-296e-4e66-987a-6584b19f9b9f"],

Cell["Check to see if V produces the correct formula:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6bdc1af9-e5f5-4dd2-b67d-0eeff7a6f3e9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"V", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1226]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5e05703b-0cf3-411a-a431-3a3601d107ac"],

Cell["\<\
Finally, verify that the derivative of V is negative along an orbit:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"31888a33-39ff-4b1d-8d81-fd947d377469"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
   RowBox[{"V", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "==", 
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "r"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[Integral]", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], "2"], 
       RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1227]:=",ExpressionUUID->"410d42bb-4271-4973-8510-a74e481b3808"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "but  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "r"}], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Prime]",
        MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "2"]}], " ", 
    "\[LessEqual]", " ", "0"}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c47e3772-cde7-48d6-b955-2396bac00cd5"],
 " as long as  r \[GreaterEqual] 0, so\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"V", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "\[LessEqual]", 
    " ", "0"}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f0b9ee53-68d5-4f5a-a77a-9f60fe43e9a9"],
 "\nTherefore, V is indeed a Liapunov function and by Theorem 3.4, the \
equilibrium point is an attractor."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398352934381*^9},ExpressionUUID->"1ad63213-d84d-4f29-985d-8e8fa1f82ec5"],

Cell["Graph the Liapunov function:   m \[Rule] 1,  k1 \[Rule] 1/10", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"08e69944-5f4a-409c-99f8-44b3cc603efc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"V", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], "/.", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"m", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", "1"}], ",", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"k1", " ", "\[Rule]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "10"}]}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1228]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5dcf03d8-51b6-4bca-8809-5f20cb64f9cb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Plot3D", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"V", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], "/.", "\[InvisibleSpace]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"m", "\[Rule]", "1"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"k1", "\[Rule]", 
         FractionBox["1", "10"]}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x1", ",", 
       RowBox[{"-", "10"}], ",", "10"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x2", ",", 
       RowBox[{"-", "4"}], ",", "4"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"AxesLabel", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<x1\>\"", ",", "\"\<x2\>\"", ",", "\"\<V\>\""}], "}"}]}]}],
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"Graphics3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"PointSize", "[", ".04", "]"}], ",", "Red", ",", 
      RowBox[{"Point", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398353276535*^9, 3.398353324344*^9}, {3.398353612866*^9,
   3.398353713442*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1229]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d16ece79-9dc8-47b7-b189-96281aeda2ad"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Example 3.7  Pendulum With Damping", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"37da462b-0c3c-42ab-a9bb-0b9a0093cd5f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Consider the resulting ODE for a pendulum with damping:\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "''"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"r", " ", "*", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "'"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"g", "/", "L"}], " ", "*", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}]}]}], " ", "=", " ", "0"}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"aa74fcbc-222f-41a2-92dd-1a21df54740a"],
 "\nWritten as a first order system: \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\t\t ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x1", " ", "=", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "\n", "\t\t ", 
     RowBox[{"x2", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "'"}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "041bbe41-ea69-4478-8220-be8bcca285b2"],
 "\n \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\t\t ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x1", "'"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", "x2"}]}], "\n", 
     "\t\t ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x2", "'"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", " ", "r"}], " ", "*", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "'"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"g", "/", "L"}], " ", "*", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}]}]}], "  ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", " ", "r"}], " ", "*", " ", "x2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"g", "/", "L"}], " ", "*", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x1", "]"}], " "}]}]}]}]}]}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"49053b4a-46ae-4f30-977a-c8d596b0e71e"],
 "\n \nEquilibrium point (just one of an infinite number of equilibrium \
points):\n  \t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1905f02c-31df-4457-966c-76aeef54b8b8"],
 " = 0\n \t \t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x2", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6d8ebd34-2975-4933-b3ab-f07a137ae204"],
 " = 0  \nLiapunov function (one choice of many is the total energy):\nTake \
the above ODE, multiply by  \[Theta] '[t], move the friction term to the rhs, \
then integrate and simplify the result:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3983522206219997`*^9, 3.398352228936*^9}, {
  3.398352939903*^9, 
  3.3983529963269997`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"02b74300-5c09-45d6-b7f8-\
63c0163e0038"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "'"}], "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], "  ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          FormBox[
           FractionBox["g", "L"],
           TraditionalForm], " ", "*", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
           RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}], "*", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], 
       RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}]}], " ", "+", " ", "constant"}], 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], "==", 
   RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", " ", "r"}], " ", "*", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], "*", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3983537406949997`*^9, 3.398353770126*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1230]:=",ExpressionUUID->"78f35724-d743-4cd3-9756-4f1b50fe6137"],

Cell["\<\
It was necessary to add a constant of integration so that the next \
requirement could be achieved.
Define the Liapunov function to be:   \[Theta] \[Rule] x1   \[Theta] ' \
\[Rule] x2\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3983522315150003`*^9, 
  3.398352233258*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e90ebf81-1830-426f-bcf1-7b2a4a51ef1c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"V", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x1_", ",", "x2_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"constant", "-", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"g", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x1", "]"}]}], "L"], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "2"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["x2", "2"]}]}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1231]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8005c514-05ae-4ebe-a2cc-df34d9a7ba24"],

Cell["Select the constant of integration so that V[0,0] = 0 ", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.39835223492*^9},ExpressionUUID->"d68810ba-3435-4524-9784-dbd0a9192087"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"constantRule", "  ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Solve", "[", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"V", "[", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], " ", ",", 
     "constant"}], "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1232]:=",ExpressionUUID->"25172ea7-283b-4ee2-8730-e89db7003b2b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"VNew", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x1_", ",", "x2_"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"V", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], "  ", "/.", 
   RowBox[{"constant", "\[Rule]", 
    FractionBox["g", "L"]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1233]:=",ExpressionUUID->"26af3634-f7ce-4957-948b-ed86e13eb328"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Then V satisfies the 3 conditions to be a Liapunov function:\n \t\t \
VNew[0,0] = 0  where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[Theta]", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "47efa775-44f9-43da-ad17-d1eeff9e18e4"],
 "= ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {"0"},
      {"0"}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5fa938a9-f2d6-4797-94c8-48be7e2616ce"],
 " is an isolated equilibrium point\n\t \t VNew[\[Theta],\[Theta] '] \
\[GreaterEqual] 0   \n\t\t ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"VNew", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}], ")"}]}], 
    " ", "\[LessEqual]", "  ", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9cdc1808-df5e-48a6-9004-b45f9593cc75"],
 "  along orbits ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     OverscriptBox["\[Theta]", "\[Rule]"],
     TraditionalForm], "[", "t", "]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1a8a5103-20ee-483a-a72a-0fedcbc68676"],
 " inside an appropriate region \[CapitalOmega]"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398353001083*^9, 
  3.398353004433*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"2f1f5d66-3928-4690-a1b0-885826bc2ace"],

Cell["In order to verify this, let:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8e35a30c-c6c1-4abb-8bc0-08929b660642"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"VNew", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x1_", ",", "x2_"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["g", "L"], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     SuperscriptBox["x2", "2"], "2"], "-", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"g", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "x1", "]"}]}], "L"]}]}], ";"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1234]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1bd9b151-7506-4913-a35d-c7dadad34752"],

Cell["\<\
Therefore VNew = 0 at the equilibrium point:  \[Theta] \[Rule] x1=0     \
\[Theta] ' \[Rule] x2=0\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b4937d7-6fbe-43fc-8876-ddd467381196"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"VNew", "[", 
  RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1235]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0cf216cf-2ee8-417b-8e69-c15085ad83b8"],

Cell["\<\
Check to see if VNew produces the correct formula as given above:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6f198a4a-6a17-453e-99c4-278ebd54a843"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"VNew", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1236]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0bdedf1e-be24-43c5-b48a-a48399827000"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Finally, verify that the derivative of VNew is negative along an orbit:  \
\[Theta][t]\nRemember to use the formula developed above:  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"VNew", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "r"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["\[Theta]", "\[Prime]",
          MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "2"], 
       RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}]}]}]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->"991345ee-ed9d-4ce1-a917-c5706bff65e8"]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cfb8b442-5037-4902-a137-0e50826a022b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
   RowBox[{"V", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "==", "   ", 
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "r"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], "2"], 
       RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1237]:=",ExpressionUUID->"793d70fe-5c22-44f0-b782-78700b3f6d96"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "but  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "r"}], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Theta]",
         FontWeight->"Bold"], "\[Prime]",
        MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "2"]}], " ", 
    "\[LessEqual]", " ", "0"}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c6059075-bac9-40b8-b5f1-813bbefc07bc"],
 " as long as  r \[GreaterEqual] 0, so\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"VNew", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", 
    "\[LessEqual]", " ", "0"}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2b03b74a-2c7e-4978-a4ed-353788bafe71"],
 "\nTherefore, VNew is indeed a Liapunov function and by Theorem 3.4, the \
equilibrium point is an attractor if the set R does not contain other \
invariant subsets other than the equilibrium point."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398353009947*^9},ExpressionUUID->"8f39e1f9-9fd2-4db4-b674-6fc75e0f6b66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Next, examine the set R: \nRemember:   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"VNew", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[Theta]", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "r"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Integral]", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["\[Theta]", "\[Prime]",
          MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "2"], 
       RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}]}]}]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0908f64a-0b00-4865-85a5-4d689fb25839"],
 "   and   \[Theta] \[Rule] x1   \[Theta] ' \[Rule] x2  \nFor this ODE,  R = \
{(x1,x2) | ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"V", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f17371e9-17d8-42c0-8889-265c79ca8644"],
 " = 0}   \n                           = {(x1,x2) | ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "r"}], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}], "2"]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e4d13eec-87bd-4833-8fb9-046635e32988"],
 " = 0}                             \n                           = {(x1,x2) | \
x2 = 0}\nThus, this set contains just the points in the phase plane on the x2 \
axis (i.e. \[Theta] ' = 0).  We have to determine if the set R has any \
invariant subsets other than the equilibrium points (i.e. are their orbits \
that start inside of R and remain fully inside of R without being one of the \
equilibrium points).  The answer to this question for this ODE is no!  To see \
why, examine the direction of the orbit which starts inside of R  (i.e.on the \
x2 axis).  The vector direction of this orbit will be given by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{"x1", "'"}]},
      {
       RowBox[{"x2", "'"}]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "866b17c0-10ad-4ef8-aebe-9802a5c7f9af"],
 ".   For an orbit to stay inside of the set R, this vector direction must \
have x2 = 0.  Thus for (x1,x2) \[Epsilon] R:\n                             \n\
\t x1' = f1[x1,x2] = x2 = 0\t\t(orbit starts on the x2 axis, x2 = 0)\n\t x2' \
= f2[x1,x2] =  - r * x2 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["g", "L"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ad7d5d83-1575-4f98-a99d-7ed82ecb6566"],
 " * Sin[x1] \n                 =  - r * 0 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["g", "L"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d9822b16-ae81-4785-a034-268b3ef8d1ff"],
 " * Sin[x1]\t\t(orbit starts on the x2 axis, x2 = 0)\n                 =  - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["g", "L"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c86aacf7-128f-4b9f-ba30-f20e97e0709b"],
 " * Sin[x1] \n                        \nTherefore,   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{"x1", "'"}]},
      {
       RowBox[{"x2", "'"}]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "bb03f77f-b227-42f2-98f2-2b1f7494dc2d"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {"0"},
      {
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", " ", 
          FormBox[
           FractionBox["g", "L"],
           TraditionalForm]}], " ", "*", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x1", "]"}]}], " "}]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "bc7dab44-2f3e-460e-99ba-a37b39da7d1d"],
 "  \nThe invariant set  R corresponds to the x2 axis.  Therefore, the \
coordinates of the points on the x2 axis correspond to: x1 = Anything and x2 \
= 0.  Note that for this orbit to remain inside an invariant subset of R:  \
that x2' must be 0 (to remain on the x2 axis).  This condition is only met \
when: \n\t\t  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", " ", 
      FormBox[
       FractionBox["g", "L"],
       TraditionalForm]}], " ", "*", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x1", "]"}]}], "  ", "=", " ", "0"}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"3f48d753-2f61-44dc-88c9-a8beaf89b6dc"],
 "\n\t\t ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x1", "]"}], "  ", "=", " ", "0"}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"985c41fc-7f61-4208-bfe9-525f795a004a"],
 "\n\t\t  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x1", "  ", "=", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[Pi]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "2"}], "\[Pi]"}], ",", " ", "..."}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"45c39c39-0918-47e3-9563-e281486eaaec"],
 "\nwhich correspond exactly to the equilibrium points:  (x1,x2) = (0,0), (\
\[PlusMinus]\[Pi],0), (\[PlusMinus]2\[Pi],0), (\[PlusMinus]3\[Pi],0), ...  . \
\nThus, by Theorem 3.4 the equilibrium point (0,0) is asymptotically stable \
because of the required behavior of both the Liapunov function and the \
invariant set R are satisfied.\n(However, ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True},
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 " all of the equilibrium points will be ",
 StyleBox["attractors",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True},
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 ":  (x1,x2) = (\[PlusMinus]\[Pi],0), (\[PlusMinus]3\[Pi],0), ...   . )\n\
Also, observe from our previous work that the stability for this point is \
only local, not global  (i.e. that \[CapitalOmega] must be defined so that \
|x1| < \[Pi]). "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3983530228129997`*^9, 3.398353057658*^9}, {
  3.398353853066*^9, 
  3.398353872841*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"dbebe988-2069-42c9-9a81-aae948b412e8"],

Cell["Graph the Liapunov function:   g->9.8,  L->1", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398352255951*^9},ExpressionUUID->"144df8ee-2937-4c28-b53e-ef684f790603"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"VNew", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], "/.", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"g", "\[Rule]", "9.8"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"L", "\[Rule]", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1238]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2642954d-cfe2-4f21-9c92-283a4e869ef9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Plot3D", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"VNew", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], "/.", "\[InvisibleSpace]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"g", "\[Rule]", "9.8"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"L", "\[Rule]", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x1", ",", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "3"}], " ", "\[Pi]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"3", " ", "\[Pi]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x2", ",", 
       RowBox[{"-", "8"}], ",", "8"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"PlotPoints", "\[Rule]", "40"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"Ticks", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", "\[Pi]", ",", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Pi]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"3", " ", "\[Pi]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"-", "\[Pi]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "\[Pi]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "3"}], " ", "\[Pi]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "Automatic", ",",
         "Automatic"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"AxesLabel", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<x1\>\"", ",", "\"\<x2\>\"", ",", "\"\<V\>\""}], "}"}]}]}],
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"Graphics3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"PointSize", "[", ".04", "]"}], ",", "Red", ",", 
      RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Point", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"n", " ", "\[Pi]"}], ",", "0", ",", 
           RowBox[{"9.8", "\[InvisibleSpace]", "+", 
            FractionBox[
             SuperscriptBox["0", "2"], "2"], "-", 
            RowBox[{"9.8", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
              RowBox[{"n", " ", "\[Pi]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"n", ",", 
          RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398354001168*^9, 3.398354019744*^9}, {3.398354053028*^9,
   3.398354068066*^9}, {3.3983540981280003`*^9, 3.398354117392*^9}, {
  3.398354393653*^9, 3.398354419251*^9}, {3.398354463439*^9, 
  3.398354465399*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1239]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2e04249e-358c-4a69-94f6-d86c6d503aac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Observe the behavior at the equilibrium points.  \n\nHowever, ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True},
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 " all of the equilibrium points will be ",
 StyleBox["attractors",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True},
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 ":  (x1,x2) = (\[PlusMinus]\[Pi],0), (\[PlusMinus]3\[Pi],0), ...   . "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398354304641*^9, 3.39835435076*^9}, {3.398354440902*^9, 
  3.39835444188*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8f9c004b-c741-4453-a6da-f8207fcdcb1c"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Example 3.3  Van der Pol Equation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a3d029a7-f05a-48f0-a41f-99a5ad2d2a49"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The next example illustrates the use of a Liapunov function other than the \
energy equation.\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x1", "'"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", " ", "x2"}]}]}], "\n", "\t", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x2", "'"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"x1", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", "*", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            FormBox[
             SuperscriptBox["x2", "3"],
             TraditionalForm], "/", "3"}], " ", "-", " ", "x2"}], ")"}], 
         " "}]}]}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0d7080c1-4f73-466e-a64a-c643f3fd7b9d"],
 "\nEquilibrium point :  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["X", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1f82f87b-4501-4a02-82ba-603128f51bd3"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["0", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8b813023-d5c6-4890-95e4-089ca068afeb"],
 " (remember: \[Alpha] < 0 \[Rule] Stable and \[Alpha] > 0 \[Rule]  Unstable)\
\nLiapunov function (one choice of many, but is NOT the total energy):   \n\t\
\t  V[x1,x2] =",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{" ", 
     FormBox[
      SuperscriptBox["x1", "2"],
      TraditionalForm]}], "2"], TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"4eaee2c7-5c78-40c6-a388-9417b7b7cf72"],
 StyleBox[" +  ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{" ", 
     FormBox[
      SuperscriptBox["x2", "2"],
      TraditionalForm]}], "2"], TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"327931a4-184f-4150-b8c4-9473596a2043"],
 "\nTherefore, the Liapunov function V satisfies the required conditions:    \
\n\t\t  V[0,0] = 0   \n\t\t  V[x1,x2] > 0   ( except at the equilibrium \
point)   \n\t \t  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"V", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      FormBox[
       OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
       TraditionalForm], "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"ead151d1-a755-4ce0-80b5-88019b9316cf"],
 " \[LessEqual] 0 (for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"],
     TraditionalForm], "[", "t", "]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "27a8d3ca-e02c-4153-9d7d-40f147d56818"],
 " \[Epsilon] \[CapitalOmega])   \nCarrying out the first and third \
requirements in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398352264343*^9, 3.398352273598*^9}, {3.398353080951*^9,
   3.398353098066*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d71aee25-8532-427a-9971-5aeb9d10fd2e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"V", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x1_", ",", "x2_"}], "]"}], " ", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{" ", 
       FormBox[
        SuperscriptBox["x1", "2"],
        TraditionalForm]}], "2"],
     TraditionalForm], " ", "+", "  ", 
    FormBox[
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{" ", 
       FormBox[
        SuperscriptBox["x2", "2"],
        TraditionalForm]}], "2"],
     TraditionalForm]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1240]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d92c6d01-8f63-434c-ad15-1994a4200257"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"V", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1241]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1e1a7f8a-f6d8-4a5c-bce6-1ecb8c741fb1"],

Cell["\<\
Thus, the equilibrium point satisfies the required condition.

Next, determined the slope of the Liapunov function in the direction of a \
orbit (i.e. a solution of the ODE).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398352276583*^9},ExpressionUUID->"a08c9ef6-24b5-4c24-8b93-3e4c1c8e4198"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
  RowBox[{"V", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1242]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a3a09785-9e21-4298-afbd-88632e0c32dc"],

Cell["Substitute the ODE:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4ac95acb-5a23-4a69-b89a-c5d78c685344"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"eq1", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
    RowBox[{"V", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "/.", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[InvisibleSpace]", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["x1", "\[Prime]",
        MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["x2", "\[Prime]",
        MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], "-", 
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          FractionBox[
           SuperscriptBox[
            RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}], "3"], "3"], "-", 
          RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}]}], 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398354499111*^9, 3.398354513646*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1243]:=",ExpressionUUID->"18df3af2-9d55-45e3-b3c9-f22f65e08885"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", " ", "eq1", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1244]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5ac9b06f-32dc-4055-a379-131ef569d5da"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is clear from this equation that V'[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["x", "\[Rule]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "31dda3a5-39fd-4919-af63-74894a709032"],
 "[t]] \[LessEqual] 0 when both: \[Alpha] \[LessEqual] 0 and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}], "2"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"26134584-ce94-4117-9d9a-e1725bd64251"],
 StyleBox[" \[LessEqual]",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " 3.  This can be used to define our open subset \[CapitalOmega] of our \
domain (this is consistent with our earlier work).\n\nThus, V[x1,x2] =",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{" ", 
      FormBox[
       SuperscriptBox["x1", "2"],
       TraditionalForm]}], "2"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "02c4a4ef-7805-43b2-81f5-54530a9219fa"],
 " +  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{" ", 
      FormBox[
       SuperscriptBox["x2", "2"],
       TraditionalForm]}], "2"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "894d6a79-3665-4b31-a1a7-7285e6c8807c"],
 " is an acceptable Liapunov function for this ODE and equilibrium point at \
the origin. Thus, if the condition on the invariant set R is also met, then \
by Theorem 3.4, the equilibrium point is an attractor. \nNext, examine the \
set R:\n \nFor this ODE,  R = {(x1,x2) | ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"V", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c00d73f3-a5fa-48df-9e7e-85c01d3721f8"],
 " = 0}   \n                           = {(x1,x2) | ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox["1", "3"]}], " ", "\[Alpha]", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}], "2"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "3"}], "+", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a923716f-9a52-4c22-87dd-e774a5bfa019"],
 " = 0}                             \n                           = {(x1,x2) | \
x2 = 0}\nThus, this set contains just the points in the phase plane on the x2 \
axis.  We have to determine if the set R has any invariant subsets other than \
the equilibrium point.  The answer to this question for this ODE is no!  To \
see why, examine the direction of the orbit which starts on the x2 axis.  The \
vector direction will be given by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{"x1", "'"}]},
      {
       RowBox[{"x2", "'"}]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f54691dd-86e0-4a05-a6ef-0a0729e3252f"],
 ".    Thus for (x1,x2) \[Epsilon] R:                             \n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\t ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x1", "'"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", " ", "x2"}], " ", "=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "\n", "\t ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x2", "'"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], " ", "=", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"x1", " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", "*", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            FormBox[
             SuperscriptBox["x2", "3"],
             TraditionalForm], "/", "3"}], " ", "-", " ", "x2"}], 
          ")"}]}]}]}]}], "\n", "        \t\t                ", 
     RowBox[{"=", "  ", "x1", "   "}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7ad1b541-af37-4d95-819a-9494f74d4419"],
 "                     \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{"x1", "'"}]},
      {
       RowBox[{"x2", "'"}]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "08531ecb-5e69-4a99-9e02-8ece9789aa3a"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
       {"0"},
       {
        RowBox[{"x1", " "}]}
      }], ")"}], "."}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "02d9128f-d686-4466-a86c-1c5d1619d5d7"],
 "   Therefore, to remain on the x2 axis then x2' = 0, and consequently x1 = \
0 ( i.e. the equilibrium point).  This condition is only met at the origin \
which is the equilibrium point. Thus, by Theorem 3.4 the equilibrium point is \
asymptotically stable. "
}], "Text",
